hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1088","Narrated Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him): A bowl (of water) was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He drank from it, and on his right side was a boy who was the youngest among the people, and the elderly were sitting on his left side. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: “O boy! Do you permit me to give this bowl to these elders before you?” He replied, “O Messenger of Allah! I would not give your leftover to anyone before myself.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave it to him."
"1089","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that (on one occasion) a goat was milked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was in the house of Anas bin Malik. Water from the well in the house of Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) was mixed into the milk. Then the cup (bowl) was given to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he drank from it. When he removed the cup from his mouth, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was on his left side and a Bedouin was on his right side. So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said—because he thought that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give his leftover drink to the Bedouin—“O Messenger of Allah! Give it to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), he is sitting next to you.” But the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his leftover drink to the Bedouin and said: “The one on the right has more right (to receive first), then whoever is on his right.”"
"1090","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not withhold water in excess of your need so that the grass may also be withheld."""
"1091","It is narrated in another narration from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do not withhold surplus water in order to prevent surplus grass."""
"1092","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath in order to unlawfully take the right of a Muslim, and he is lying in that oath, will meet Allah while Allah is angry with him."" Then Allah revealed this verse: ""Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price..."" until the end of the verse (Aal-e-Imran: 77). At that moment, Sayyiduna Ash'ath (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived and said, ""Abu Abdur Rahman (i.e., Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him), what are you narrating to you? This verse was revealed concerning me. I had a well in the land of my cousin (he claimed the well as his property until the matter was brought before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: 'Present your witnesses (to prove that the well is yours).' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah! I have no witnesses.' So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Then an oath will be taken from the other party.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah! He will immediately swear an oath.' On this occasion, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated this hadith, and Allah the Exalted revealed this noble verse to confirm the words of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"1093","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""There are three types of people whom Allah will neither look at on the Day of Resurrection nor purify them (from their sins), and for them is a severe punishment: (1) A person who has surplus water while on the road but withholds it from a traveler in need; (2) A person who pledges allegiance to an Imam only for worldly gain—if he is given something of this world, he is pleased, but if he is not given, he is displeased; (3) A person who, after the Asr prayer, stands to sell his goods and swears by Allah—besides whom there is no deity—that he paid such and such a price for it, and someone believes him (and buys it). Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) recited this verse: 'Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price...' to the end of the verse. (Aal-e-Imran: 77)"""
"1094","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man was walking when he was overcome by thirst, so he went down into a well and drank water from it. Then he came out and saw a dog panting and licking wet earth due to severe thirst. The man said (to himself), 'This dog has suffered thirst just as I have.' So he went down into the well again, filled his sock with water, held it in his mouth, climbed up, and gave the dog water to drink. Allah accepted this deed of his and forgave him."" The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there a reward for us in serving animals?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes! There is a reward in serving every living (moist-livered) creature."""
"1095","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There are three types of people with whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look at them (with mercy): (1) The person who swears an oath on his wealth that he has given more than he actually has, and he is lying; (2) The person who, after Asr, swears a false oath to seize a Muslim's property; (3) The person who has more water than he needs, but does not give it to others. Allah will say (to him on the Day of Resurrection): 'Today I withhold My bounty from you just as you withheld surplus water from people, which you did not create.'"""
"1096","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, (on the Day of Resurrection) I will drive away some people from my Hawd (Al-Kawthar) just as stray camels are driven away from the water trough."""
"1097","Sayyiduna Sa'b bin Jathamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for anyone except Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) to declare a pasture (to prohibit grazing or hunting there)."" (The caliph is also the representative of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him.)"
"1098","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The horse is a source of reward for some people, a means of protection for some, and a cause of sin for others. So, the person for whom it is a source of reward is the one who keeps it (the horse) in the way of Allah (for jihad), then ties it with a long rope in a pasture or garden. For every area of the pasture or garden that the horse roams, he will receive good deeds in return. And if the horse’s rope breaks and it jumps over one or two elevations, then its steps and its droppings will all be counted as good deeds for him. And if the horse passes by a stream and drinks from it, even though the person did not intend to let it drink from that stream, he will still receive good deeds. Thus, such a horse is a source of reward for this reason. And the person who keeps a horse to avoid begging and to earn money, and he does not forget Allah’s right in his own self and in his riding, then this horse is a means of protection (i.e., safety) for that person. And the person who keeps a horse merely for pride, showing off, and enmity towards the Muslims, then that horse will be a burden for that person.” And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about keeping donkeys, so he said: “Nothing has been revealed to me regarding them except this comprehensive and unparalleled verse: ‘So whoever does an atom’s weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom’s weight of evil will see it.’” (Surah Az-Zalzalah: 7-8)"
"1099","(Amir al-Mu’minin) Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I received a she-camel as booty on the day of Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me another she-camel as well. So one day, I made both of those she-camels sit at the door of an Ansari, and I intended to load them with izkhir (a type of grass) so that I could sell it, and at that time, a goldsmith from Banu Qaynuqa’ was also with me, and I wanted to take his help for the wedding feast (walima) of Sayyida Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her). And (Sayyiduna) Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him) was at that time drinking wine inside that house. There was a singing woman with him, and she was singing: “Get up, Hamza! For the fat, fresh, young she-camels.” So he took a sword and turned towards both of those she-camels, and he cut (split) their humps and ripped open their bellies, then took out their livers. (Sayyiduna) Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I saw such a scene that terrified me, then I went to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and at that time (Sayyiduna) Zaid bin Haritha (may Allah be pleased with him) was also with him. So I narrated this news to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came out. Accordingly, Sayyiduna Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) and I went along with him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to them and became very angry with them. Then (Hamza), in that state of intoxication, raised his eyes and said, “You people are nothing but the slaves of my forefathers.” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back on his heels and left from there, and this incident occurred before the prohibition of wine (and music)."
"1100","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to allot land in Bahrain to the Ansar, but the Ansar said, ""(We will not take it) unless our Muhajir brothers are given the same."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon you will see others being preferred over you after me, so be patient until you meet me."""
"1101","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever buys date-palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruits will belong to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. And whoever buys a slave and the slave has some property, that property will belong to the seller, unless the buyer has stipulated otherwise."
